! The `ph.x` input that generated `reference.out.ph-o2-fixed-lsda-phonon`.
!
!   pw.x -in o2-fixed-lsda.in && ph.x -in o2-fixed-lsda-phonon.ph.in
!
! `o2-fixed-lsda.ph.in`'s twin with `trans = .true.`: the Gamma dynamical
! matrix of a spin-polarized system, which is the quantity
! `defumat.response.phonon` refuses for nspin = 2. `ph.x` allows it -- there is
! no LSDA refusal anywhere in `phq_readin.f90` or `phq_setup.f90`; what those
! refuse is noncollinear magnetism (`:546`, `:777`, `:807`), `i_cons` (`:850`),
! two Fermi levels with a metal (`:854`) and `lraman`/`elop` with an ultrasoft
! or PAW dataset (`:811`, `:814`, `:817`).
!
! The cell is the same triplet O2: fixed occupations at tot_magnetization = 2,
! so it stays magnetic exactly rather than demagnetizing the way the
! antiferromagnetic hydrogen chain does, and it is an ultrasoft insulator, so
! it exercises the two terms P39 added (becsumort and the multiplier matrix)
! in the spin-polarized regime as well.
Gamma dynamical matrix of triplet O2, LSDA
 &inputph
  tr2_ph = 1.0d-14,
  epsil = .true.,
  trans = .true.,
  fildyn = 'o2-phonon.dyn',
  amass(1) = 15.99994,
 /
0.0 0.0 0.0
